---
import mcpData from '../data/mcp-tools.json';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/docs-layout.astro';

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'endpoint', text: 'Endpoint and authentication' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'tools', text: 'Tool catalogue' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'call', text: 'Calling a tool' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'console', text: 'Console automation' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'scoping', text: 'Scoping API keys' },
];
const curl = `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer nbk_..." \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -H "Accept: application/json, text/event-stream" \\
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list","params":{}}'`;
const call = `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer nbk_..." \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"project_apply","arguments":{
    "name":"mcp-smoke",
    "nodes":[{"name":"sw1","template":"Ethernet switch"},{"name":"sw2","template":"Ethernet switch"}],
    "links":[{"a":"sw1","b":"sw2"}]
  }}}'`;
const exec = `{
  "id": "<node uuid>",
  "commands": ["show ip interface brief"],
  "timeoutMs": 8000,
  "prompt": "Switch[>#]\\\\s*$",
  "terminalLengthZero": true
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="MCP & agents"
  description="The stateless MCP endpoint, its tool catalogue, contract-derived schemas, and API-key scoping."
  headings={headings}
>
  <header class="docs-page-head">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow">Automation</p>
    <h1>MCP &amp; agents</h1>
    <p class="docs-lede">
      {mcpData.tools.length} tools over Streamable HTTP. Names, schemas, and authorization come from the
      same contract as the HTTP API; MCP calls run through the same middleware and audit path.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-prose">
    <h2 id="endpoint">Endpoint and authentication</h2>
    <p>
      <code>POST /mcp</code> speaks JSON-RPC 2.0 over Streamable HTTP (stateless). It supports
      protocol versions <code>2025-06-18</code>, <code>2025-03-26</code>, and
      <code>2024-11-05</code>. Authenticate with an API key: <code>Authorization: Bearer nbk_…</code>.
      Send <code>Accept: application/json, text/event-stream</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      A key needs <code>mcp.use</code> plus the privileges of the tools it should call. Effective
      scopes are the intersection of the key's scopes and the owner's current privileges, so revoking
      a grant narrows every key the user holds.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-demo__code" style="border:1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius:2px;">
      <button class="inline-flex h-7 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 rounded-sm px-2.5 text-[0.8rem] font-medium whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted hover:text-foreground h-6 px-2 text-xs" data-copy={curl}>Copy</button>
      <pre><code>{curl}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <h2 id="tools">Tool catalogue</h2>
    <p>
      Read-only tools cover lists, gets, status, export, and stats. Destructive tools are deletes,
      clears, and applies. The table is generated from
      <code>apps/controller/src/mcp/tools.ts</code> and the contract summaries.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-table-scroll">
    <table aria-label="MCP tools">
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Procedure</th><th>Access</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          mcpData.tools.map((tool) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{tool.name}</code></td>
              <td><code>{tool.procedurePath}</code></td>
              <td>
                {tool.destructive ? 'destructive' : tool.readOnly ? 'read-only' : 'mutating'}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-prose">
    <h2 id="call">Calling a tool</h2>
    <p>
      Arguments are the procedure input, unchanged. Tool results carry the same structured content as
      the HTTP call. The example applies a two-switch lab; repeating it with the returned
      <code>projectId</code> updates rather than duplicates.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-demo__code" style="border:1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius:2px;">
      <button class="inline-flex h-7 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 rounded-sm px-2.5 text-[0.8rem] font-medium whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted hover:text-foreground h-6 px-2 text-xs" data-copy={call}>Copy</button>
      <pre><code>{call}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <h2 id="console">Console automation</h2>
    <p>
      <code>console_exec</code> runs commands against a serial or telnet console and returns the
      transcript with <code>ok</code> and <code>timedOut</code>. VNC-only nodes have no command
      console. <code>console_reset</code> clears a stuck proxy.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-demo__code" style="border:1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius:2px;">
      <button class="inline-flex h-7 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 rounded-sm px-2.5 text-[0.8rem] font-medium whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted hover:text-foreground h-6 px-2 text-xs" data-copy={exec}>Copy</button>
      <pre><code>{exec}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <h2 id="scoping">Scoping API keys</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Create keys in <strong>Profile → API keys</strong> or with <code>auth.apiKeys.create</code>; the plaintext is shown once.</li>
      <li>Give a lab agent <code>project.read</code>, <code>node.read</code>, <code>link.read</code>, and <code>node.console</code> for read-and-inspect work.</li>
      <li>Add <code>project.write</code>, <code>node.create</code>, <code>node.update</code>, <code>node.files</code>, <code>link.write</code>, and <code>drawing.write</code> for apply.</li>
      <li>Project-restricted keys must pass <code>projectId</code> to apply; resolving a project by name needs global <code>project.write</code>.</li>
      <li><code>sessionOnly</code> procedures never accept API keys, including key creation and session revocation.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="docs-callout" data-tone="warn">
      <span class="docs-callout__label">Destructive tools</span>
      <p>
        <code>project_apply</code> with <code>prune: true</code> deletes unlisted nodes, links, and
        keyed drawings. Treat it like a delete in client confirmation policies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
